k  individuals would be uh you know feel  safer and would feel like they would be  able to  enjoy the experience knowing that you  know the entirety of the venue was  at tested three-night show outside the  city national grove in anaheim  each car had an assigned parking space  off to one side  a tailgate zone outside that zone  everyone wore  face masks at the bathroom there was a  temperature check  jordan harding is the venue's general  manager we don't want anybody that's  coming here to to get sick  but ultimately you know we've created an  environment where people can be  contained and safe and socially  distanced we've done the best we can but  we acknowledge  that you know there is some risk  involved to minimize that risk  fans could use a mobile app to order  food drinks  and merch all delivered right to their  parking spot  we literally parked our car and we have  our blocked off space so  i feel pretty safe we wouldn't go to  concert indoors right now so this is  perfect  [Music]  alt rock music often rebels in  surprising ways  but at the drive-in concert mcmahon's  fans conformed  they followed the rules you know i know  that that sounds like a crazy thing at a  rock and roll show to be like yay for  following the rules but  in this particular case if we want to be  able to do this we have to  to protect each other and be good  citizens like rock music  fans have to prove they can adapt  we're calling that the honcore it may be  the only way  live music has an encore in covet  america  for cbs this morning mark strassman  atlanta  i love the encore it's just so great to  see live music and people out there in  any form i do love the idea of the merch  and the beverages being delivered to  your car i love all of it if i had a  horn right now i'd be honking it i hope  that sticks around  long after the pandemic
 

